Description: createsuperuser: use the --password option
 The option is parsed but never read: the non-interactive path always creates
 the account with an empty password, so `--noinput --password=...` yields an
 account that cannot log in. Without the option the account gets an unusable
 password (set_password(None)), as the --noinput help text describes.
Author: dionysius <dragon.dionysius@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
--- a/seahub/seahub/base/management/commands/createsuperuser.py
+++ b/seahub/seahub/base/management/commands/createsuperuser.py
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@
             except exceptions.ValidationError:
                 raise CommandError("Invalid email address.")
 
-        password = ''
+        password = options.get('password', None)
 
         # Try to determine the current system user's username to use as a default.
         try:
